{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891439-the-black-fomorian-dream","id":891439,"title":"The Black Fomorian Dream.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-15T16:37:23-07:00","id":891439,"title":"The Black Fomorian Dream.","content":"When it comes to the Fomorians, there is details about what each Court represents, what sort of Dreaming (Nightmare?) might result from their victory over the forces of Arcadia. White is treacherous, deceitful, and inhuman, Red is violent, bloody, and insane, and Green is alien, inscrutable, and enigmatic.<br /> <br /> But there is posited another dream. One paragraph is all I have found about it, but the Black Court of Fomorians is described to exist. It claims that they may represent the combined force of all three of the other courts, but that they never existed during the War of Trees. So.... when did they come together to form this group? Or do they exist separate?<br /> <br /> If the Black Court is separate, then what do theyou represent? What &quot;Dream&quot; do they espouse? Has anyone used them, and if so, how?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11773-shining-imperator","name":"Shining Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T05:43:24-07:00","id":891680,"title":"","content":"I don't remember that. Do you know what book and page number talks about the Black Court?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr 