\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891439-the-black-fomorian-dream?p=969951#post969951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fomorians are the ancient primordial rulers of the world with immeasurable power imprisoned for all eternity by the Tuatha de Daanan. Fomori are some random dudes possessed by a minor spirit and easily torn to shreds by werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Just putting out there how similar a Changeling is to a Drone, Kami, Gorgon, Formori but of the Dreaming from a werewolf perspective. If one wanted to point out some connection the possessed don't have to be by &quot;minor&quot; spirits. So a Changeling balor might have been a true force to be reckoned with and thus why the werewolves call anything remotely close to him.. Formori.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T16:39:59-07:00","id":970306,"title":"","content":"Admittedly, there was a bit of snark in my response. I actually enjoy Werewolf: The Apocalypse quite a bit; I'm just sick of the Fomorian/Fomori question that feels like comes up in every single thread where the Fomorians are mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T16:47:12-07:00","id":970308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/891439-the-black-fomorian-dream?p=970306#post970306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, there was a bit of snark in my response. I actually enjoy Werewolf: The Apocalypse quite a bit; I'm just sick of the Fomorian/Fomori question that feels like comes up in every single thread where the Fomorians are mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It does! Espcially when the majority of Fera use the right and proper term &quot;bakemono&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> But I like to think the Formorians So frightened the werewolves in the ancient past anything monster posssed they name after them because &quot;HOLY Shit athat was scary&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}